From 6df3af4f82bb9c00ea2d5b0ef79427af66ecbf8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QED64 Toolchain <qed64-toolchain@localhost>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 16:55:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: resident stdin ring + PROXY_TO_PTHREAD (browser64
 transport port)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Run the real 'lean --worker' main loop on the application pthread:
-sPROXY_TO_PTHREAD=1 (the 24-thread pool absorbs the proxy slot), and a
futex-based stdin ring in shared wasm memory so the loop's blocking
reads are legal without occupying the outer runtime Worker. The outer
worker mallocs control words + a byte ring, calls
lean_browser64_configure_input_ring before callMain, then writes LSP
frames and Atomics.notifies the wake word; stdin reads drain the ring
with exact-fill semantics (Lean's readJson reads Content-Length bytes
in one Stream.read — a short non-EOF read would corrupt framing).
stdout/stderr and every other file keep Emscripten's normal path.
lean_main's FS setup and the getenv shim proxy to the JS main thread
(MAIN_THREAD_EM_ASM*): under a proxied main they otherwise run on a
pthread with no FS/ENV. The pump-mode exports are untouched — both
transports coexist in one binary.

Ported from browser64's lean4-resident-transport.patch (contract
org.lean-browser64.resident-transport/v1); its module.cpp/compact.cpp
hunks remain on the backlog as separate patches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
